"""Offline barrier for scrapers/livingcompound/run.py — the theme's swapped state/city rows, the
price postfix as the ONLY period word, the licence/age/halls columns, the amenities, and the oracle.

Every HTML fragment below is VERBATIM livingcompound.com markup captured live on 2026-09-24, trimmed
to the blocks the code reads (the <body> tag, <h1>, the price span, the detail/address <li> rows —
first occurrence of each key —, the Features card, the Description card and two gallery anchors):
  · P9543_* — /property/al-nahda-villa/ («SAR 85,000 / Year», Rega Ad License No 7200654129);
  · P9746_* — /property/luxury-fully-furnished-1-bhk-apartment-ruwais-… («SAR 5,000 / Month»);
  · P9927_* — a villa priced «SAR 185,000» with NO postfix;
  · P9951_* — a page whose type and status rows are absent;
  · P9843_* — a page with a status but no type row.
The functions under test are the production ones; only to_catalog / find_district_in_text are
stubbed. Two tests replace ONE word inside a verbatim row to reach a branch the live site did not
exhibit on capture day («For Sale», «Sold»), and say so.

WHAT IT PINS
  1. IDENTITY: ad_number = LCP + the WordPress post id read from the body class.
  2. LOCATION: «Province/State» is the CITY and «City/Town» is the DISTRICT on this theme.
  3. PERIOD = SOURCE: «/ Year» → annual, «/ Month» → monthly ×12, no postfix → NULL with the figure
     unconverted. «For Sale» → price_total. Sold/Rented → skipped.
  4. REAL COLUMNS: licence, halls, property_age (from Year Built), area from «121 m2», bedrooms.
  5. AMENITIES: the unit's own Features chips → True; «Close By …» stays NULL; «Air-Condition» maps.
  6. PII redacted; photos are the gallery's zoom anchors.
  7. ORACLE: /?p=<id> → 404 gone; a landed page carrying postid-<id> live (Sold label → gone); 403 → law.
  8. main(): the skip tally reaches end_run(notes=...); prune only after a complete enumeration.
"""
